title The closed room leads with what stands
prompt autonomous lap -- the baton, Lindy first, crux first, in the prose lane
rota lap 4946, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; law and boundary, read through touch. The lap walked the register fence line and pressed each post: door_over_ceiling read 0 and held, and the reading that gave way was the one no roster held -- front_doors_unrostered_over at 17, a boundary the diagram drew and no hand could find.
think The card's agent-doable queue is four reds, none of them prose and none of them mine. My lane is the front doors, so the air lap's fence walk is the register meter: run it, and read which posts stand.
think prose_register_scan prints three populations. Two are held -- DOOR at 20 percent, teaching at a ceiling of 4. The third, front_doors_unrostered_over, is counted and gated by nothing on purpose: a page that agreed to no ceiling must never red the tree. It read 17.
think Crux first inside that 17, by measurement rather than taste. counsel/README.md read 50 percent, the worst of them, and git grep answered 10 living citers, the most of them. One page carried both extremes.
think The page was never badly written; its subject is a closure, so it said closed, never, nothing, no longer. Meter is uncapped because refusal is its subject -- and a front door is Door, and a door leads with what is.
think Eleven sentences restated, each keeping its claim: nothing here is retired became every piece here stands exactly as filed; closed means no longer growing, never no longer true became closed names a room that has stopped growing and keeps every word it holds true; the propose-never-seat coinage moved into backticks, which is how this tree writes a seated term and what the meter reads past.
obs Two figures on the page were FREE and nothing held them -- 764 dated pieces and 1,977 inbound references, both typed once and left. Measured this lap: the shelves hold 772. So the page now names the two commands and says RUN rather than READ, which is the fifth thing Gauge asks a figure to carry.
obs Paying the page onto the enforced roster is the point rather than a flourish. A sweep alone leaves the reading free to drift back; the roster line is the fence post, and door_setting_declared rose 18 to 19 with undeclared still 0, so the page now answers its own ceiling to a reader who never opens the scan.
obs The teaching-tier ratchet was left alone. Its three over-target pages sit in manual/ and edu/yonder/, two lanes away, and one bounded change is the lap.
loom register=counsel_readme before_percent=50 after_percent=12 sentences=24 negatives=3
loom roster=prose_register door_documents=20 door_over_ceiling=0 unrostered_over_before=17 unrostered_over_after=16
loom qa=counsel_readme composite=90 letter=A truth_mode=judged service=92 shadow=85
file counsel/README.md the closed room's front door, swept 50 percent to 12 and its two free figures replaced by the commands that answer them
file tools/fixtures/p/prose_register_scan.sh one DOOR roster entry, so the swept page is walled rather than merely tidy
file construction/fleet-claims.kyri the claim opened and pushed before the build, then closed on landing
recommend keep-going -- sixteen unrostered front doors stand above the ceiling; press/README.md at 27 percent with 9 citers is the next crux by the same two measurements
scope one front door swept and rostered; one fixture roster line; no module, wire, or store touched
